seg-0f28d1a1163f = The engine’s { "2610" } s is not that 1-σ time, and should not be. <c1/> is the first { "10" } s grid point (<c2/>) at which <em>this seeded realisation’s</em> absolute phase error exceeds { "20" } ns (<c3/>). A random walk’s first crossing of a level often comes well before the time its 1-σ envelope reaches that level, and the realisation also carries the residual frequency error the filter is left with after the { "600" } s sync. So the law fixes the scale, a few thousand seconds for a { "3" }×{ "10" }⁻¹⁰ clock against { "20" } ns, not the exact value. The test asserts a <b>{ "2000" }–{ "3200" } s band</b> around it, not the number.

